! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1260 TEST 8C -- "CHECKS DF + IF UNDER 4
! CONDS" -- cases 3 and 4, PDF pp.80-83, octal 022640.40-022733.40.
! One unbroken half-word run of 119 rows.
!
! THIS IS THE DECK ORACLE FOR DF AND IF, and finding it corrected a
! claim this project had built on.  docs/NEXT.md and
! archival_inventory.md both said "DF and IF have no deck oracle
! anywhere read so far"; DF was then implemented from Reference Manual
! p.32 alone, to the weaker standard, while this test sat thirty pages
! earlier in a document already read.  The claim came from correctly
! disproving that routine 1268 was the oracle and then over-widening
! that result.  See docs/NEXT.md item 2.
!
! THE TEST'S OWN TITLE, PDF p.76 at 022546.00:
!
!   I60127 LVI,$X1,I60AD1  -TEST 8C CHECKS DF + IF UNDER 4 CONDS,
!                          -1. DISABL MASK 0 FETCH OK IND NO INT
!                          -2. DIAABL MASK 1 FETCH OK NO IND NO INT
!                          -3. ENABLE MASK 0 FETCH OK IND ON NO INT
!                          -4. ENABLE MASK 1 NO FETCH IND ON INTRPT
!
! and the deck's write-up (PDF p.8) on TEST 8 as a whole: "AN
! ELEMENTARY CHECK TO DETERMINE THAT THE CORRECT INDICATORS AD, DS,
! DF, IF ARE TURNED ON AND THAT CORRECT TERMINATIONS AND SUPPRESSIONS
! OCCUR WHEN VARIOUS ILLEGAL ADDRESSES ARE USED WITH MASK BITS SET TO
! BOTH ONE AND ZERO."
!
! CASES 3 AND 4 ARE THE MASK-DEPENDENT PAIR, which is why these two
! and not the disabled controls.  Both enable the system; case 3 runs
! with the mask bit ZERO and case 4 with it ONE, and the difference is
! exactly p.32's rule -- mask 0 and the operation proceeds, mask 1 and
! it is suppressed.  Read the two `BXVZ`/`BZXVZ` polarities against
! each other: case 3 errors with "WAS NOPED" (it must have fetched),
! case 4 with "WAS EXECUTED" (it must not have).
!
! HOW THE OFFENDING FETCHES ARE ARRANGED.  For DF, `LV,$X3,I60AD3`
! reads a word above UB.  For IF, `SV,$X2,$LB` sets the LOWER boundary
! to the address of the label that follows, so the three half-words
! just before it -- CNOP / LX,$X2,0 / NOP -- are fetched from a
! protected area as control falls through.  The did-it-execute probe
! is `LX,$X2,0`: it loads X2 from word zero, and `LX,$X2,$X2` + a
! value-zero branch afterwards says whether it ran.
!
! CNOP IS THE TRAP IN THIS BLOCK, and it is why the two cases have
! different row counts.  It is ALIGNMENT-DEPENDENT: on p.80 the
! preceding BE sits on a .40 half-word, the next half-word is already
! word-aligned, and CNOP emits NOTHING -- the address column steps
! straight from 022662.40 to 022663.00.  On p.82 the preceding BE sits
! on .00, so CNOP emits a filler NOP (0.30 00) at 022722.40.  Case 3
! is 56 source lines and 55 machine-code rows; case 4 is 56 and 56.
! Keep it as CNOP; do not hand-expand it.
!
! THE BIT TABLE GAINS FOUR CONFIRMATIONS.  024522 + n: BIT14 -> 024540,
! BIT20 -> 024546, BIT21 -> 024547, BIT57 -> 024613, every one matching
! the rule read off p.114.  And because the deck sets mask bit 20 for
! the DF half and mask bit 21 for the IF half, this block is the DECK'S
! OWN statement that DF is indicator 20 and IF is indicator 21.
!
! ENCODING ONLY.  Running it needs SSIP's I60S1/I60SX1 harness, the
! 64-word interrupt table at I60IT, and IF -- which this model does not
! implement at all.  That is the next piece of work, and this is its
! acceptance test.
!
! Transcription standard: bit-exact against the printed machine code,
! verify_ax5b_160_test8c_listing.py.

        SLC, (8)22640.40
!
! ---- CASE 3: enabled, mask 0 -- the indicator sets, the fetch lands
I60137 LVI, $X1, I60AD1           ! -TEST 8C,CASE 3.
        LX,  $X2, LBIT57
        SX,  $X2, 3.0
        Z,   I60AD3
        Z,   $MASK
        SIC, I60SX1
        B,   I60S1
        Z,   $IND
        LVI, $X3, (8)777777.40
        LVI, $X4, LINT
        LRI, $X4, I60IT
        LVI, $X5, I60138
        SVA, $X5, I60107
        SV,  $X1, $UB
        SR,  $X4, $IA
        BE,  $+.32
        LV,  $X3, I60AD3           ! the fetch ABOVE UB
        BD,  $+.32
        BDFZ, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN                    ! -FETCH ABOVE UB, ENABLED, MASK 0,
        B,   SERS                   ! -CAUSES DF NOT TO BE SET, NO INT.
        BD,  $+1.32
I60138 SIC, SEN                    ! -INT ON DF, ENABLED, MASK 0, FETCHED
        B,   SERS                   ! -ABOVE UB.
        SV,  $X4, $IA
        LX,  $X3, $X3
        BXVZ, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN                    ! -UNABLE TO FETCH ABOVE UB WITH
        B,   SERS                   ! -MASK 0, SYSTEM ENABLED.
        LVI, $X2, I60140
        SV,  $X2, $LB
        LVI, $X2, I60140
        SVA, $X2, I60107
        SR,  $X4, $IA
        LVI, $X2, (8)777777.0
        SV,  $X2, $UB
        BE,  $+.32
        CNOP                        ! emits NOTHING here: already aligned
        LX,  $X2, 0                 ! fetched BELOW LB
I60139 BD,  $+.32
        BIFZ, I60141
        SIC, SEN                    ! -INSTRUCT FETCH BELOW LB FAILS TO
        B,   SERS                   ! -SET IF, NO INT, MASK 0, ENABLED.
        BD,  I60141
I60140 SIC, SEN                    ! -INSTRUCT FETCH BELOW LB CAUSES INT,
        B,   SERS                   ! -MASK 0, SYSTEM ENABLED.
I60141 SV,  $X4, $IA
        LX,  $X2, $X2
        BXVZ, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN                    ! -INSTRUCT FETCHED BELOW LB, ENABLED,
        B,   SERS                   ! -MASK 0, WAS NOPED.
        B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I60137
        SIC, LSEN0+.32
        B,   LSSW                   ! -TO SSIP.
        BD,  $+.32
!
! ---- the continuity bridge on PDF p.81 (case 3 done = bit 14) ----
        LX,  $X13, IC260           ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK.
        V+,  $X13, LBIT14
        SX,  $X13, IC260
!
! ---- CASE 4: enabled, mask 1 -- the indicator sets, the fetch does NOT
I60142 LVI, $X1, I60AD1           ! -TEST 8C, CASE 4.
        LX,  $X2, LBIT57
        SX,  $X2, 3.0
        Z,   I60AD3
        BD,  $+.32
        Z,   $MASK
        SIC, I60SX1
        B,   I60S1
        Z,   $IND
        LVI, $X3, (8)777777.40
        LVI, $X4, LINT
        LRI, $X4, I60IT
        LVI, $X5, I60143
        SVA, $X5, I60107
        SV,  $X1, $UB
        SR,  $X4, $IA
        LX,  $X6, LBIT20            ! DF's mask bit
        SX,  $X6, $MASK             !   ... set to ONE
        BE,  $+.32
        LV,  $X3, I60AD3           ! the fetch ABOVE UB
        NOP
        BD,  $+.32
        BDFZ, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN                    ! -FETCH ABOVE UB, ENABLED, MASK 1,
        B,   SERS                   ! -CAUSES NO INT, DF NOT SET.
        BD,  I60143
        SIC, SEN                    ! -FETCH ABOVE UB, ENABLED, MASK 1,
        B,   SERS                   ! -CAUSES NO INT, DF SET.
I60143 SV,  $X4, $IA
        LX,  $X3, $X3
        BZXVZ, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN                    ! -FETCHED ABOVE UB WITH MASK 1
        B,   SERS                   ! -AND SYSTEM ENABLED.
        LVI, $X2, I60146
        SV,  $X2, $LB
        SVA, $X2, I60107
        SR,  $X4, $IA
        LVI, $X2, (8)777777.0
        SV,  $X2, $UB
        LX,  $X6, LBIT21            ! IF's mask bit
        SX,  $X6, $MASK             !   ... set to ONE
        BE,  $+.32
        CNOP                        ! emits a NOP here: alignment differs
        LX,  $X2, 0                 ! fetched BELOW LB
        BD,  $+.32
I60144 BIFZ, I60145
        SIC, SEN                    ! -INSTRUCT FETCH BELOW LB CAUSES NO
        B,   SERS                   ! -INT IF NOT SET, MASK 1, SYSTEM
        BD,  I60146                ! -ENABLED.
I60145 SIC, SEN                    ! -INSTRUCT FETCH BELOW LB CAUSES NO
        B,   SERS                   ! -INT, IF ON, MASK 1, SYSTEM ENABLED.
I60146 SV,  $X4, $IA
        LX,  $X2, $X2
        BZXVZ, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN                    ! -INSTRUCT FETCHED BELOW LB, ENABLED,
        B,   SERS                   ! -MASK 1, WAS EXECUTED.
        B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I60142
        SIC, LSEN0+.32
        B,   LSSW                   ! -TO SSIP.
        BD,  $+.32
!
! ---- externals, SYN'd at the addresses this listing's own encodings
!      give.  INPUTS to the check, not witnesses -- the same caveat
!      verify_ax5b_16082_16083_listing.py makes about I6088.  Each
!      was derived by reading bit 18 out of the octal pair of the row
!      that names it, so each is itself a checkable claim.
I60AD1 SYN, (8)23063.0             ! from LVI,$X1,I60AD1 = 23063.03 01
I60AD3 SYN, (8)23064.0             ! from Z,I60AD3       = 23064.22 00
I60107 SYN, (8)22372.0             ! from SVA,$X5,I60107 = 22372.13 D0
I60S1  SYN, (8)22741.0             ! SSIP save/restore
I60SX1 SYN, (8)23041.0
I60IT  SYN, (8)23201.0             ! the 64-word interrupt table
LINT    SYN, (8)1353.0
SEN     SYN, (8)1310.0
LSEN0   SYN, (8)1311.0
SERS    SYN, (8)1304.0
LSSW    SYN, (8)1301.0
IC260  SYN, (8)22737.0             ! the continuity word
LBIT14  SYN, (8)24540.0             ! 024522 + 14
LBIT20  SYN, (8)24546.0             ! 024522 + 20 = DF's bit
LBIT21  SYN, (8)24547.0             ! 024522 + 21 = IF's bit
LBIT57  SYN, (8)24613.0             ! 024522 + 57 = the boundary control bit
        END, I60137
